Every query sorts the folders, and a sort marked the database changed, so
`zoxide query` wrote the whole file each time it ran. Whatever watches the
file for changes, as the launcher's Recent does, then reads it again and
writes it again, without end. Nothing reads the order a sort leaves on
disk, since every reader sorts again, so a sort no longer marks it; what
a query removes still does.

